# Cursor Background Agent Configuration for Gmail Unsubscribe Tool

## Project Overview
This is an AI-powered Gmail unsubscribe tool that uses DeepSeek API to automatically unsubscribe from promotional emails.

## Agent Tasks

### 1. Email Processing Agent
- Monitor Gmail for new promotional emails
- Process unsubscribe requests automatically
- Generate daily reports of unsubscribed emails
- Clean up old screenshots (older than 7 days)

### 2. Maintenance Agent
- Check for dependency updates weekly
- Monitor API rate limits
- Validate authentication tokens
- Clean up log files

## Project Structure
```
/src
  /ai - DeepSeek AI integration
  /auth - Gmail authentication
  /automation - Puppeteer browser automation
  /email - Email fetching and management
  /unsubscribe - Unsubscribe logic
```

## Key Commands
- `npm start` - Run the unsubscribe tool
- `npm run agent:process` - Process emails in background
- `npm run agent:cleanup` - Clean up old files
- `npm run agent:report` - Generate unsubscribe report

## Environment Variables Required
- `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` - DeepSeek API key for AI processing
- `CLIENT_ID`, `CLIENT_SECRET` - Gmail API credentials
- `AUTO_CONTINUE=true` - For background processing
- `DELETE_AFTER_UNSUBSCRIBE=true` - Auto-delete emails

## Agent Guidelines
1. Never commit sensitive data (.env, token.json)
2. Always validate email content before processing
3. Take screenshots for audit trail
4. Handle rate limits gracefully
5. Log all operations for debugging

## Error Handling
- Retry failed unsubscribes up to 3 times
- Log errors to `logs/error.log`
- Send notifications for critical failures
- Gracefully handle API rate limits

## Safety Rules
- Never delete emails without successful unsubscribe confirmation
- Always maintain audit trail with screenshots
- Respect rate limits for both Gmail and DeepSeek APIs
- Process maximum 50 emails per session by default
